## Things the librarian's report missed (3)

1. **`GDK_BACKEND=x11` silently breaks this.** If you have `GDK_BACKEND=x11` in any environment file (`.bashrc`, systemd user unit, etc.), GTK4 uses XWayland. On XWayland, a non-decorated window may not get the ARGB visual. Run the smoke test under `env -u GDK_BACKEND` if you have it set anywhere.

2. **`glib::idle_add_local` runs every frame tick — you don't need it for v1.** The `connect_realize` empty region is sufficient for "transparent overlay, click-through when idle." Add the idle helper only when you actually need to gate input on a popup. Don't ship v1 with the idle loop.

3. **The `set_input_region` call must be re-issued after every surface (re-)configure.** Mutter may renegotiate buffers (e.g. on DPI change, monitor add/remove). The smoke test won't hit this, but the gnome-ocr production path should call `set_input_region` again from `connect_surface_state_changed` or after `connect_configure`. For v1 you can skip this — Mutter rarely reconfigures overlay-class windows.

