    engine = None;
    recognising = false;
    // forget the grant so the portal asks again
    if let Ok(mut stored) = restore_token.lock() { *stored = None; }
    // open a new capture with the picker
    ...same as Start but with token None...
}
```

Hmm, I can factor the "open the capture" into a helper to avoid duplication.

Let me restructure the pipeline's Start handling into a function:

```rust
fn open(runtime, restore_token, japanese_only, shutdown) -> Result<(Capture, Option<String>, Engine)>
```

Hmm, let me keep it simpler. Let me extract the capture-opening into a small closure/function inside `run`:

```rust
let open_capture = |runtime: &Runtime, token: Option<String>| -> Result<(Capture, Option<String>)> {
    runtime.block_on(crate::capture::start(token))
};
```

Hmm, closures with borrow issues. Let me just write a helper fn:

```rust
fn open_capture(
    runtime: &tokio::runtime::Runtime,
    token: Option<String>,
) -> anyhow::Result<(Capture, Option<String>)> {
    runtime
        .block_on(crate::capture::start(token))
        .context("start screen capture")
}
```

And then both Start and ChangeSource use it.

Let me write the pipeline's command handling:

```rust
Ok(Command::Start) => {
    if capture.is_none() {
        let token = restore_token.lock().ok().and_then(|t| t.clone());
        match open_capture(&runtime, token) { ... }
