GLib format specifiers: `%b` = abbreviated month name, `%e` = day of month (space-padded), `%l` = hour 12-hour no leading zero, `%M` = minute, `%p` = AM/PM.

So `"%b %e %l:%M %p"` → "oct 24  8:16 pm" (with %e padding).

