**layout.rs**:
```rust
/// A block of text that had not been seen before, and whether it starts a
/// new paragraph.
#[derive(Debug, Clone)]
pub struct Fresh {
    /// The block itself.
    pub block: Block,
    /// Whether the page has a large gap between this block and the block
    /// before it in the page, so it starts a new paragraph.
    pub new_paragraph: bool,
}
```

And `join_blocks`:
```rust
/// Joins the blocks into text.
///
/// Where the page has a large gap between two of them, the break is kept and
/// the next block is set out with an ideographic space, which is how a
/// paragraph is marked in Japanese.
pub fn join_blocks(blocks: &[Fresh]) -> String {
    let mut text = String::new();
    for (index, entry) in blocks.iter().enumerate() {
        if index > 0 {
            text.push('\n');
            if entry.new_paragraph {
                text.push(IDEOGRAPHIC_SPACE);
            }
        }
        text.push_str(&entry.block.text());
    }
    text
}
```

And `Layout` needs to produce the flags. Let me add:
```rust
impl Layout {
    /// Whether the block at the given place starts a new paragraph, which is
